       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe, and I'd like you to confirm or correct it first.\n\n- **Single dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum single oral dose of ibuprofen, which is 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times daily is 6400 mg/day. The maximum for adults in a monitored setting is 3200 mg/day, and the OTC limit is 1200 mg/day. At 6400 mg/day the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially.\n\nHere are some common regimens you may have meant:\n- 400 mg PO every 6 hours (1600 mg/day), for mild to moderate pain or fever\n- 600 mg PO every 6 hours (2400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2400 mg/day), the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions\n- 1600 mg total per day, split into smaller doses\n\nIf 1600 mg/day was the intended total, tell me the per-dose amount and frequency, for example 400 mg four times daily. If you really do want the original dose, please confirm that and I'll enter it with a note recording that you verified it."
